Modified by MultiPak through 2026-11-11. This runtime requires an explicit instance
ID and stores its state separately from the system Waydroid installation.
Changes cover per-instance paths, D-Bus names, LXC names, binderfs devices,
networks, image release selection and desktop entries. Session mount sources
are derived from authenticated identities; private Android data is separated
from the APK/icon exchange, and desktop sockets are pinned before mounting. Hardware-specific
global service operations are disabled in this experimental runtime.

The named-instance architecture was informed by Waydroid PR #1990:
https://github.com/waydroid/waydroid/pull/1990
The old PR patch is not applied directly to this source tree.

SELinux image mount labeling follows the Fedora Waydroid package:
https://src.fedoraproject.org/rpms/waydroid
Only existing policy types are used; no additional SELinux policy module is
installed. A local file-context mapping assigns the existing waydroid_data_t
type to the private data and exchange directories on hosts with that policy.

